# Code Review - Operation Flow Trace Rule

This rule extends the main code review rule (`code-review.mdc`) for
operation tracing tasks.

## Activation

Triggered when user requests trace of a specific user operation, e.g.:
- "魚を売却するフローをトレースして"
- "操作: 銀行から金を引き出す"
- "Trace the operation: ATM withdrawal"

## Required Output (in addition to §0 confirmed files)

For each traced operation, output:

### Flow Diagram

```
[Entry Point] User action description
  ↓ <file>:<line> (<function_name>)
  ↓ Event/call: <event_name or function call>
[Next Stage] What happens
  ↓ <file>:<line> (<function_name>)
  ↓ State change: <variable / DB / UI>
...
[Exit] Final state
```

### State Changes Table

| Stage | Variable | Before | After | Persistence |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | xPlayer.money | 1000 | 1500 | DB updated |
| 2 | inventory['fish'] | 5 | 4 | DB updated |

### Failure Paths

| Trigger | Where caught | Response |
|---|---|---|
| Not enough money | server/main.lua:120 | notify("not_enough_money") |
| Invalid amount | server/main.lua:115 | early return |

### Network Round-trips

Count: N (client→server: X, server→client: Y)

## Confidence Requirements

Same as main rule:
- Every step must have file path + line number
- Tag with `[確認済]` if directly read
- Tag with `[推測]` only with stated reasoning
- Stop if `[推測]` exceeds 30%
